    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1528">

                <pb facs="1655" n="1641" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">831.24/12–3043</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Liaison Officer</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to Mr. Bainbridge C.
                            Davis, Division of North and West Coast Affairs</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-30">December 30, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Davis</hi>: Referring to your memorandum of
                    December 29, 1943<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1528-f1"/> and your request for
                    additional information concerning Lend-Lease<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1528-f2"/>
                    and other military assistance extended to Venezuela, there is set forth
                    hereafter the latest available information on this subject supplementary to the
                    detailed data furnished you a few weeks ago:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Air and Ground Material</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">Dollar Value of Lend-Lease<lb/>Equipment furnished
                    Venezuela<lb/>(As of September 30, 1943)</p>
                <table cols="5" rows="2">
                    <row>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Original Lend-Lease allotment</hi> (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">Agreement between Dept. of State and
                                LA</hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d1528-f3"/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Representative</hi>)</cell>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Dollar value of “Floated” material</hi><anchor
                                n="*" xml:id="d1528-f4"/> (<hi rendition="#italic">Shipping
                                Ticket</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">as of 30 Sept. 1943</hi> (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">Air and Ground</hi>)</cell>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Percent of total received</hi>
                        </cell>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Amount yet to be allotted Amount</hi>
                        </cell>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Percent</hi>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>$15,000,000</cell>
                        <cell>$l,441,822<anchor n="†" xml:id="d1528-f5"/>
                        </cell>
                        <cell>10%</cell>
                        <cell>$13,558,178</cell>
                        <cell>90%</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Naval Material</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">Lend-Lease Credit</p>
                <table cols="2" rows="2">
                    <row>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Estimated Value on Completion</hi> (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">As of November 22, 1943</hi>)</cell>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Value of Deliveries to August 31, 1943</hi>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell role="num">$1,061,787</cell>
                        <cell role="num">$334,934<anchor n="†" xml:id="d1528-f6"/>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>In addition to the foregoing, the Navy Department has under consideration the
                    possibility of leasing six 83 foot vessels to Venezuela the value of which
                    totals $660,000.</p>
                <pb facs="1656" n="1642" xml:id="pg1642"/>
                <p>The Navy Department may desire to lease only three of these vessels in which case
                    their value would amount to $330,000.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Military and Naval Missions to
                        Venezuela</hi>
                </p>
                <p>On March 24, 1941 an Agreement was signed between the Governments of Venezuela
                    and the United States,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d1528-f7"/> which provides for a
                    United States Naval Mission. So far as we know this mission (composed of 5
                    officers and several enlisted men) is performing very satisfactorily.</p>
                <p>Negotiations are about to be concluded for the signing of an Agreement for a
                    United States Military Aviation Mission to Venezuela.</p>
                <p>One Venezuelan National is now attending the United States Naval Academy (entered
                    in 1943).</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Orme Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1528-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1528-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1528-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1528-f2-content">
                <p>For text of the Lend-Lease Agreement between the United States and Venezuela,
                    signed March 18, 1942, see <ref target="frus1942v06#pg_739">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1942, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi>, p. 739</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1528-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1528-f3-content">
                <p>Presumably Lend-Lease.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1528-f4" n="*" xml:id="d1528-f4-content">
                <p>“Floated” material signifies equipment which has been shipped out of the U. S. A.
                    [Footnote in the original.]</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1528-f5" n="†" xml:id="d1528-f5-content">
                <p>Note: On 1/14/43, Mr. Kempter of FEA (Lend Lease) stated that cumulative $ value
                    of Ld. Lease exports through 8 Spt. 1943 was $1,465,000 (= air, ground naval,
                    &amp; Treasury Procurement items) according to his “official” Ld. Lease figures.
                    RA/B. C. Davis. [Footnote in the original.]</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1528-f6" n="†" xml:id="d1528-f6-content">
                <p>Note: On 1/14/43, Mr. Kempter of FEA (Lend Lease) stated that cumulative $ value
                    of Ld. Lease exports through 8 Spt. 1943 was $1,465,000 (= air, ground naval,
                    &amp; Treasury Procurement items) according to his “official” Ld. Lease figures.
                    RA/B. C. Davis. [Footnote in the original.]</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1528-f7" n="4" xml:id="d1528-f7-content">
                <p>Department of State Executive Agreement Series No. 203; 55 Stat. (pt. 2)
                    1235.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
